n a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=(4t-7){e}^{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293147 1113 #uuid "c26d8c3c-e107-52ba-89a9-ccc2af1eaed1" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293147 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-7){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293149 13194139534525 true] [17592186293148 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534525 true] [17592186293148 1041 "field-1" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293148 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293149 13194139534525 true] [17592186293148 1110 #uuid "21660576-1240-5665-a5f3-e25ef9579462" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293149 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293149 1111 #uuid "dd79ef94-fcdf-58f6-aa30-5aa511cb311b" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293151 13194139534525 true] [17592186293150 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534525 true] [17592186293150 1041 "field-2" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293150 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293151 13194139534525 true] [17592186293150 1110 #uuid "45b0bf94-741a-59b3-b780-9aa3