c{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}+5) \\\\  & =20{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a(t)=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=0.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =5(0)^{4}+5 \\\\  & =0+5 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=0,$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=5.$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293159 13194139534525 true] [17592186293158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534525 true] [17592186293158 1041 "field-1" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293159 13194139534525 true] [17592186293158 1110 #uuid "9883c0c2-64e6-59f0-a592-6d80b6d75371" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293159 1034 "0" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293159 1111 #uuid "b799486a-3a34-5012-8eb2-40d2060c035a" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293161 13194139534525 true] [17592186293160 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534525 true] [17592186293160 1041 "field-2" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293160 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293161 13194139534525 true] [17592186293160 1110 #uuid "38e1fde2-d1f3-5faa-8af2-8a854a4a24d0" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293161 1034 "5" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293161 1111 #uuid "46b58199-f9d9-567b-bfaf-99cd1a368168" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293163 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1089 "q-4771" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1100 "The position $x(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-10t-2,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the time at which the particle is stationary." 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1113 #uuid "24413cc5-0267-5920-b89f-10f793534ebf" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293162 1145 "First, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-10t-2) \\\\  & =2t-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m/s}.$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-10 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =10 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293164 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293165 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293166 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293167 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293168 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1041 "selection" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293166 13194139534525 true] [17592186293163 1110 #uuid "d05e1821-bf10-52dd-b786-afb9afa67640" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293164 1034 "t=7\\,\\text{s}" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293164 1111 #uuid "c528b48f-fdbf-5397-b017-50d5926ff5c3" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293165 1034 "t=8\\,\\text{s}" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293165 1111 #uuid "0a8c6717-d882-5d52-a491-71cffae3080e" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293166 1034 "t=5\\,\\text{s}" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293166 1111 #uuid "0bfa9dab-4042-5177-b960-f74d772f577f" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293167 1034 "t=2\\,\\text{s}" 131