ae6d59811" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293176 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive.\n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is $(\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293178 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293179 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293180 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293181 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293182 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1041 "selection" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293178 13194139534525 true] [17592186293177 1110 #uuid "7b20ae87-2caa-5a0e-81f0-bb93426cd586" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293178 1034 "(\\frac{3}{4},\\infty )" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293178 1111 #uuid "23b1fbde-50c2-5d53-b5a1-85d5f81fba1f" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293179 1034 "(4,\\infty )" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293179 1111 #uuid "a58f6864-c59b-5bdc-b124-ec8f5452cad1" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293180 1034 "$[0,\\frac{5}{3})$ and $(\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534525 true] [17592186293180 1111 #uuid "fee1eebf-f311-55a9-9222-2595f1919cf7" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293181 1034 "(2,\\frac{13}{4})" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293181 1111 #uuid "21a8c3c8-b06e-51dc-8f8f-6f18677bbf62" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293182 1034 "[0,\\frac{5}{6})" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293182 1111 #uuid "3b6afbe4-d16e-5d05-9fc4-d7aab17e979a" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293184 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1089 "q-7188" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1113 #uuid "e823f661-78ed-5c49-931f-9f7b092bd2fe" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293183 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{9}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+14t+17) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}+6t+14) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\frac{4}{3}t+6 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}t & =6 \\\\ t & =4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=4.5.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(4.5)=-\\frac{2}{3}(4.5)^{2}+6(4.5)+14=27.5.\n$$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293184 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293185 13194139534525 true] [17