m the origin at this time." 13194139534525 true] [17592186293190 1113 #uuid "a2ee9a7a-96f8-5c1a-98bc-31a0726aad61" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293190 1145 "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to calculate the velocity function. We can do that by taking the derivative of the position function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+8) \\\\  & =2t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when $v=0$ So, we set $v=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-2 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =2 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the particle is stationary only at $t=1.$ To find the displacement from the origin at this time, we substitute $t=1$ back into $s(t)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s(1) & ={1}^{2}-2(1)+8 \\\\  & =1-2+8 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary at $t=1$ and its displacement from the origin at this time is $7.$" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293192 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293193 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293194 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293195 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293196 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1041 "selection" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293195 13194139534525 true] [17592186293191 1110 #uuid "a8d351ef-39f4-5dae-94d8-3aeaa48f46a4" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293192 1034 "t=2,\\,s=8" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293192 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293192 1111 #uuid "64a51385-11d7-51c7-a2d4-7659fb60ca51" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293193 1034 "t=3,\\,s=9" 13194139534525 true] [17592186293193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534525 true] [17592186293193 1111 #uuid "e5251bd4-427b-5273-8a5d-2b9